        "source": "arxiv",
        "caption": "A sketch of the universe's expansion rate as a function of time in our model. More details on each of the four stages (relaxation, phase transition in the NEC-violating sector, violation of the NEC, inflation/reheating) as well as on the notation used are provided in the following sections.",
        "filename": "introfig.png"
      },
      {
        "key": "3b697080958f7c024e538cb0f45ce718",
        "url": "https://inspirehep.net/files/3b697080958f7c024e538cb0f45ce718",
        "source": "arxiv",
        "caption": "The slope of the potential as a function of the effective dark energy $V=-\\lambda_1^3\\phi_1+\\Lambda_\\star$. The green region corresponds to the allowed window, compatible with both the slow-roll dynamics and classical evolution. Adjusting the slope so as to make it optimally compatible with both requirements (blue curve) inevitably entails fine tuning. A change in the initial c.c.~of the order of $\\Lambda_\\star$ leads to a breakdown of the slow-roll regime before the cosmological constant relaxes to sufficiently low values (red curve). The case corresponding to a constant slope is depicted by the horizontal purple line. The figure is not to scale and we have set $\\mpl$ to one.",
        "filename": "fig1_lasma2.png"
      },
